    "/* ---- reclaim runtime: bitmap slab + holder counts + regional sweep [rt:head] ----\n",
    " *\n",
    " * Three of the four tiers the runtime provides (release the whole local place, zero the counts, regional sweep):\n",
    " *\n",
    " *   local    the parse region bump-allocates; leaving the scope rewinds the bump pointer, O(1);\n",
    " *   counts   holder counts attach only to **pointer assignment**; reaching zero returns the slot to the free chain at once;\n",
    " *   sweep    once a region's occupancy crosses the pressure line, mark from the roots + registration bitmap, then **scan 64-bit words in order** and free the unmarked ones.\n",
    " *\n",
    " * Shape: a payload rounds up to a slot in **8-byte** units (not a power of two: an 80-byte object takes an 80-byte slot), laid out contiguously in\n",
    " * EXTC_RC_SLAB_BITS-aligned slabs. Finding the slab from an object pointer is **one bitwise AND** (alignment means no table lookup);\n",
    " * finding the slot number is **one reciprocal multiply and shift** (see extc_rc_slotOf). Each slab has three\n",
    " * bitmaps (occupancy / mark / cross-region registration) + one holder count and one type number per slot; free slots are chained by slot number,\n",
    " * so allocation is O(1). The sweep does not chase pointers and does not free slot by slot.\n",
    " *\n",
    " * Soundness obligations (missing one dangles, so these are not optimizations):\n",
    " *\n",
    " *  1. **A fresh slot and a slot whose old value is overwritten are two operations.** A fresh slot holds the next free slot number; dereferencing that as an old pointer crashes;\n",
    " *     the compiler knows statically which it is, so there are two entry points: initRef only writes and bumps the target count, storeRef reads the old value.\n",
    " *  2. **The registration bitmap is persistent and deduplicated; the sweep does not clear it.** Clearing it forgets cross-region in-edges, and the next round frees objects that another region\n",
    " *     still points at.\n",
    " *  3. **Counts saturate in three stages, and the saturated value means unknown.** At the ceiling the count sticks and never decreases again, so it is never mistaken for zero; hand those to the sweep.\n",
    " *  4. **Marking walks pointer fields with the object's own type descriptor.** The allocation site hands the descriptor to the runtime with the slot (each slot stores one\n",
    " *     pointer); walking with the wrong descriptor, or treating a missing one as present, misses marks.\n",
    " *  5. **Releasing a slot must clear its registration bit.** Otherwise a new object reusing the slot looks live through the stale entry and is missed.\n",
    " *  6. **Only slots allocated by this runtime may be counted/registered/marked.** A pointer from a plate/pool/stack/C allocation is not such a slot;\n",
    " *     the bitwise AND in slabOf lands in unrelated memory, which segfaults. Every slab is entered at creation into a table sorted by base address,\n",
    " *     and count/register/mark first ask owns; a slot absent from the table (or already free) is skipped entirely.\n",
    " *  7. **When the host cannot be proved, the target region must leave the sweep.** The cross-region registration sits on the target and the source object does not know it,\n",
    " *     so it cannot be withdrawn; the static root table has no such slot either. Then mark the target's region as not swept (rather collect less),\n",
    " *     and never sweep as usual with incomplete seeds -- the entry point is `extc_rc_storeRefUnknown`.\n",
    " *\n",
    " * Two further criteria:\n",
    " *  - marking stops at an object outside the region and **does not write its mark bit** -- an object of another region left marked makes its\n",
    " *    next sweep skip it and free its children. Anything outside the region counts as live.\n",
    " *  - assigning a data field calls neither inc nor dec; only a change of reference touches a count.\n",
    " *\n",
    " * One boundary: counts move only on **in-edges**. When a slot reaches zero and is released, the targets it pointed at reach zero only after the emitter drops them\n",
    " * before the object dies (clear the field / unlink the chain); counts not dropped wait for the sweep to kill that section as a whole. This is on\n",
    " * the rather-collect-late side: a dead object only keeps others alive a little longer; it never dangles.\n",
    " *\n",
    " * Self-containment: this text depends only on <stdint.h> <stddef.h> <stdlib.h> <stdio.h>\n",
    " * and <string.h> (memset/memmove), already included at the top of the generated file, and names no user type (the allocation site hands the type layout to the runtime through an ExtcRcType\n",
    " * descriptor); every symbol is static.\n",
    " */\n",
    "\n",
    "#ifndef EXTC_RC_SLAB_BITS\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_SLAB_BITS 19   /* 512 KiB blocks: a block is issued to slots whole (no tail hole), and a bigger block spreads the per-slab header,\n",
    "                                  * the three bitmaps and one mmap over more slots, which is worth ~6% of the alloc-heavy sizeratio shape and costs\n",
    "                                  * nothing on the pointer-chasing shapes; 512 KiB keeps every class under the uint16 slot-number limit. */\n",
    "#endif\n",
    "#ifndef EXTC_RC_FLOOR\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_FLOOR ((int64_t)1 << 20)\n",
    "#endif\n",
    "#ifndef EXTC_RC_SCALE_MAX\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_SCALE_MAX ((int64_t)1 << 40)\n",
    "#endif\n",
    "/* Retreat factor after an empty sweep: one round finds nothing, so this whole-heap mark buys zero garbage; retreat hard.\n",
    " * The base is 2 (trigger line = max(2x live, floor)) times this factor, so one empty sweep puts the line at 8x the live set: a shape with a large live set\n",
    " * and little garbage skips a whole-heap mark that would trade the live set for a few MB; a shape with plenty of garbage\n",
    " * collects next round, which resets the factor to 0, so it only affects loads that really have no cycles. */\n",
    "#ifndef EXTC_RC_SCALE_MUL\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_SCALE_MUL ((int64_t)4)\n",
    "#endif\n",
    "#ifndef EXTC_RC_HOLD_SAT\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_HOLD_SAT 65535u\n",
    "#endif\n",
    "/* Per-component counting is off by default: the counting entry point is a no-op so no call site pays an increment.\n",
    " * The next section redefines it as a real increment when counting. */\n",
    "#if !EXTC_RC_TIME\n",
    "#define EXTC_RC_TICK(k) do { } while (0)\n",
    "#endif\n",
    "\n",
